From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek Sahu <abhsahu@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 07:17:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: battery: clear consumer dependencies
 after successful probe

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167300

Some platforms declare _DEP on a battery device for unrelated
consumers. On those systems the consumer driver's probe keeps
returning -EPROBE_DEFER because adev->dep_unmet for the consumer
never drops to zero.

acpi_dev_clear_dependencies() walks the consumer list and decrements
each consumer's dep_unmet counter. The ACPI core invokes it
automatically for ACPI scan handlers via acpi_scan_attach_handler(),
but a provider that ships as a platform_driver has to call it
explicitly from its probe path -- there is no acpi_scan_handler and
no .attach where the core could do it on the provider's behalf. This
battery driver is registered as a platform_driver whose
acpi_battery_probe() does not do that today, so a successful battery
probe currently leaves consumer dependencies pending forever.

Call acpi_dev_clear_dependencies() at the end of acpi_battery_probe()
when initialization has succeeded, so any device that legitimately
depends on the battery can finish enumerating.

Signed-off-by: Abhishek Sahu <abhsahu@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-02128
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-bos@97dda421e745f76b51d9df9781f57b6a7e31e5f6
---
 drivers/acpi/battery.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/battery.c b/drivers/acpi/battery.c
index 70b0470777f0..2926903e0af6 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/battery.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/battery.c
@@ -1325,6 +1325,15 @@ static int acpi_battery_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (result)
 		goto fail_pm;
 
+	/*
+	 * Some platforms declare _DEP on a battery device for unrelated
+	 * consumers. This driver is registered as a platform_driver whose
+	 * .probe path does not auto-clear consumer dep_unmet counters on
+	 * success, so do it explicitly here to allow those consumers to
+	 * probe once the battery is up.
+	 */
+	acpi_dev_clear_dependencies(device);
+
 	return 0;
 
 fail_pm:
